  * syscall stub in pc and its caller in lr/bt.
  *
  * First sample 90 s after start, then every 120 s, 40 samples at most.
+ *
+ * A profiler too: `sysctl kern.sweetprof=N` takes N samples 50 ms apart of the threads of the same
+ * processes that run or wait for a core ("PRF name thread-id pc ... lr ... bt ..."), and once the
+ * header lines ("SMP name[pid] slide ... mh ...") and the executable files mapped below the shared
+ * region ("PRF img name start size file-offset path") to symbolicate them. Where the CPU time goes
+ * while CoreAnimation draws.
  */
